<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia central bank chief denies moving to IMF.</title>
<headline>Indonesia central bank chief denies moving to IMF.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's central bank governor Sudradjad Djiwandono denied on Wednesday he planned to resign take up a job with the International Monetary Fund (IMF).</p>
<p>&quot;It's the first time I heard about it,&quot; Djiwandono said in reply to a reporter's question during a briefing ahead of the annual bankers' dinner in Jakarta on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Djiwandono said it was not true that he was looking for a residence in Washington because he was about to resign from Bank Indonesia and join the IMF.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no such thing like that,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
